committer zichuanxu <zichuanxu28@gmail.com> 1790796357 +0900

D0full: truncate per source, keeping small sources whole, instead of newest-first over all records

Above the cap the largest source (by cost) is cut to its newest records that fit what the other
sources leave, and every other source is given whole. If the sources other than the largest already
exceed the cap, the newest-first rule over all records applies and is counted apart
(`truncation` "newest"; "source" for the per-source cut, "none" when everything fits). Under the
newest-first rule alone vip_sender lost every contact card (the oldest records) behind its e-mail;
now it keeps all cards and cuts only e-mail.

The item note records, per declared source, the records given and left out (`by_source`) and the
case (`truncation`), replacing `dropped_by_source`; the estimator reports `newest_first` and the
records left out per source. The cell's pin is updated; the pins of the existing cells are not
touched and pass unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
